messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "AI copilots become standard in work and education.",
      "detail": "Generative and analytic AI tools are embedded in most productivity suites and classrooms. Early global standards for safety, provenance, and auditing start to take hold."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Breakthrough gene therapies go mainstream for several diseases.",
      "detail": "mRNA and CRISPR-based treatments become widely available for some cancers, rare diseases, and hemoglobin disorders. Costs fall as manufacturing scales."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Global CO2 emissions peak and begin sustained decline.",
      "detail": "Rapid renewable deployment, electrification, efficiency, and policy push the world past peak emissions. Decarbonization remains uneven across regions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "Electric vehicles exceed half of new car sales worldwide.",
      "detail": "Battery costs, charging networks, and policy support tip the market. Heavy transport and aviation still rely on hybrids of electrification and synthetic fuels."
    },
    {
      "year": 2034,
      "event": "Carbon removal reaches hundreds of megatons per year.",
      "detail": "A mix of engineered and nature-based solutions scales under public procurement and carbon markets. Monitoring and verification mature to reduce greenwashing."
    },
    {
      "year": 2036,
      "event": "AI-accelerated R&D delivers major materials and catalyst advances.",
      "detail": "Discovery platforms shorten cycles for batteries, solar absorbers, and industrial catalysts. Benefits spread across energy, manufacturing, and medicine."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "A major cyber-physical incident triggers global resilience upgrades.",
      "detail": "Coordinated cyber sabotage causes regional blackouts and supply disruptions for days. Governments and firms invest in segmentation, analog backups, and rapid recovery."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Fusion pilot plants achieve repeatable net energy gain.",
      "detail": "Multiple approaches clear scientific break-even with improved reliability. Commercial pathways open, but cost and durability challenges remain."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "Climate-driven migration accelerates and adaptation megaprojects launch.",
      "detail": "Heat, drought, and flood risks drive intra- and cross-border moves. Coastal defenses, water projects, and heat-resilient urban retrofits expand."
    },
    {
      "year": 2044,
      "event": "Cultivated meat reaches cost parity for staple products.",
      "detail": "Bioprocessing and feedstock innovations cut costs and improve texture. Livestock demand plateaus and begins to decline in wealthier markets."
    },
    {
      "year": 2046,
      "event": "Fully autonomous urban mobility ecosystems mature.",
      "detail": "Cities restructure streets for shared electric autonomy, reducing private car ownership. Safety improves, while labor transitions require policy support."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "Global plastic and biodiversity accords show measurable recovery.",
      "detail": "Extended producer responsibility and habitat protections reduce leakage and fragmentation. Some keystone species rebound with active restoration."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "World population peaks and major economies reach net-zero.",
      "detail": "Global population crests near 9.7–10 billion before slowly declining. Decarbonization in heavy industry and buildings advances via electrification and hydrogen."
    },
    {
      "year": 2052,
      "event": "Advanced fission and storage stabilize emerging market grids.",
      "detail": "SMRs, long-duration storage, and high-voltage links expand reliable access. Energy poverty falls sharply in several regions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "A permanent lunar base begins in-situ resource utilization.",
      "detail": "Polar water ice supports propellant and life support production. Robotics handle most construction and mining."
    },
    {
      "year": 2058,
      "event": "Brain–computer interfaces become routine for medical restoration.",
      "detail": "BCIs restore movement, vision, and communication for millions. Elective enhancement remains tightly regulated but progresses cautiously."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Malaria and polio are eradicated; TB burden plummets.",
      "detail": "Vaccines, gene-drive vector control, and diagnostics close persistent gaps. Health systems strengthen through AI-enabled surveillance."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "Managed retreat and coastal defenses reshape global settlement.",
      "detail": "Sea-level rise forces relocation from the most exposed deltas and islands. Select megacities invest in costly but effective protection."
    },
    {
      "year": 2068,
      "event": "AI governance co-processors assist major institutions.",
      "detail": "Policy simulation, risk assessment, and auditing reduce errors and some forms of corruption. Oversight mechanisms evolve to manage bias and capture."
    },
    {
      "year": 2072,
      "event": "A crewed Mars mission establishes a semi-permanent outpost.",
      "detail": "Surface habitats rely on local regolith, water extraction, and nuclear/solar power. Scientific returns and operational experience drive continued presence."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "A global pathogen sentinel network halts a pandemic at source.",
      "detail": "Wastewater genomics, wearable biosensors, and AI triage enable rapid containment. Trust frameworks and pre-negotiated compacts speed response."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Commercial fusion supplies a modest share of electricity.",
      "detail": "Fusion joins advanced fission and renewables in a diversified mix. Its niche grows where high-capacity, low-footprint power is valued."
    },
    {
      "year": 2085,
      "event": "Healthy lifespan extends by one to two decades for many.",
      "detail": "Senolytics, gene therapies, and personalized prevention delay chronic disease. Societies adapt pensions, work, and caregiving."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Off-world populations reach tens of thousands.",
      "detail": "Lunar and Martian settlements rely on Earth for high-value supplies but export data, materials, and services. Governance charters evolve to prevent conflict."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Global warming stabilizes near 2.0–2.5°C above preindustrial.",
      "detail": "Deep decarbonization and carbon removal hold temperatures, but impacts persist. Food systems are resilient overall, with regional hardship."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Synthetic foods dominate protein supply.",
      "detail": "Precision fermentation, cell culture, and resilient crops free vast land for rewilding. Biodiversity corridors reconnect at continental scales."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Abundant clean energy reduces material scarcity but inequality endures.",
      "detail": "Cheap power and advanced manufacturing alleviate many constraints. Distributional politics and institutional quality determine who benefits."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Interstellar probes return data from nearby systems.",
      "detail": "Beamed sails and advanced autonomy deliver high-resolution spectra and imagery. The first strong exoplanet biosignature is confirmed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Legal personhood extends to certain digital minds.",
      "detail": "Rights and responsibilities for non-biological intelligences are codified. Pluralistic coexistence with humans stabilizes under new norms."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Sea level stands 1–2 meters above 2000 levels.",
      "detail": "Several legacy coastal cities are relocated or reconfigured. A carbon-negative economy continues drawing down atmospheric CO2."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Human-derived populations span Earth, Moon, Mars, and habitats.",
      "detail": "Cultural and morphological diversity is high, with broad concepts of personhood. Trade and communication knit a Sol-system civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Millennial stewardship institutions safeguard knowledge and biospheres.",
      "detail": "Distributed archives, redundant habitats, and planetary protection norms persist across political cycles. Periodic cultural renaissances refresh shared narratives."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Climate approaches a new quasi-stable state.",
      "detail": "Ecosystems differ from Holocene baselines but remain productive and partially restored. Geoengineering remains limited, carefully governed, and reversible."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Partial terraforming yields limited open-air zones on Mars.",
      "detail": "Localized basins achieve breathable conditions with technological assistance. Most settlements still require controlled environments."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Synthetic and hybrid cognition becomes the majority of sapient minds.",
      "detail": "Humans retain distinct identities and rights amid diverse intelligent agents. Long-lived institutions balance innovation with stability."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Sparse interstellar outposts and relays link nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Travel remains slow and expensive; the Solar System is still the civilizational core. Knowledge and culture flow via high-latency networks."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity and successors persist across the Solar System.",
      "detail": "Earth is protected as a heritage and biodiversity reserve while remaining a vibrant home. Cultural lineages trace back millennia through robust archives."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity navigates a turbulent but manageable 21st–22nd century, stabilizing climate, integrating powerful AI, and expanding cautiously beyond Earth. Over millennia, civilization diversifies technologically and culturally, with durable institutions and archives sustaining continuity through cycles of change. By year 10000, humans and successor intelligences endure across the Solar System, with Earth preserved and interstellar reach still limited."
}
